  "semantic_review": [
    "apply.ts persists originalIntent inside the existing applicationAttempt transaction before domain dispatch. It binds exact original request including case version, normalized full PreparedChange, unique choice, review binding and installation/project/principal/policy/access revision.",
    "Recovery requires the original intent and canonical receipt proof; material/choice mutation and duplicate identity refuse. No receipt after durable reservation remains indeterminate; no automatic redispatch.",
    "prepared-apply.ts keeps the same single domain+receipt transaction and checks originalIntent when an existing outer attempt is present. Definitive receiptVersion/grant failure returns commit:false before installing staged domain or receipt.",
    "Shared receiptProofMatches validates raw authoritative receipt, unique match, namespace, domain scope, target, principal, state incarnation and proof value. Receipt binding v1/key/public receipt shape remain unchanged.",
    "Generic recovery of legacy attempts without originalIntent is unavailable(original-intent-unverifiable); it does not synthesize historical intent. Direct canonical raw-receipt reader/producer contract remains distinct.",
    "Unrelated legitimate case edits may survive recovery; receipt reconciliation remains a separate case transaction and is never a global domain+case commit."
